  "solution": "**Given: **(27 + 15) × 2 - (95 ÷ 5) + 25 × 4 - 135 = 62\n\n [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/f1931e71405220ed05a8ca769b89c454607921ced9cf0aa43d7e1e97b0ab120f.png] \n\nLogic: **Interchange should be done of entire number and not individual digits of a given number.**\n\n**Given Equation: **(27 + 15) × 2 - (95 ÷ 5) + 25 × 4 - 135 = 62\n\nLet's check options one by one.\n\nOption 1) 2 and 4\n\n⇒ (__**27 + 15)**__ × 4 - (__**95 ÷ 5**__) +__** 25 × 2**__ - 135 = 62\n\n⇒__** 42 × 4**__ - 19 + 50 - 135 = 62\n\n⇒ __**168**__ - 19 + __**50 **__- 135 = 62\n\n**⇒ 218 - 19 - 135 = 64 ≠ 62**\n\nOption 2) 25 and 27\n\n⇒ (__**25 + 15**__) × 2 - (__**95 ÷ 5**__) + __**27 × 4**__ - 135 = 62\n\n⇒ __**40 × 2**__ __**- 19**__ + 148__** - 135 **__= 62\n\n⇒__** 80**__ - 154 + __**148**__ = 62 \n\n**⇒ 228 - 154 = 74 ≠ 62**\n\n**Option 3) 95 and 135**\n\n⇒ __** **____**(27 + 15)**__ × 2 - __**(135 ÷ 5**__) + __**25 × 4**__ - 95 = 62\n\n⇒ __**42 × 2**__ - 27 + 100 - 95 = 62\n\n⇒ __**84**__ - 27 __**+ 100**__ - 95 = 62\n\n**⇒ 184 - 27 - 95 = 62**\n\nOption 4) 5 and 15\n\n⇒ (__**27 + 5**__) × 2 - __**(95 ÷ 15**__) + __**25 × 4**__ - 135 = 62\n\n⇒ __**32 × 2**__ __**- 6.33**__ + 100__** - 135**__ = 62\n\n⇒__** 64**__ - 141.33 + __**100 **__= 62\n\n**⇒ 164 - 141.33 = 22.67**\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"Option 3\".",
